  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "The reproducible generator creates at least 75,000 encounters across at least 8,000 fictional patients, 12 fictional centers, and 18 months with all approved factors, missingness, site effects, and drift.",
    "Patient-separated chronological train, calibration, and test partitions keep the final test set untouched until model and calibrator freeze.",
    "Leakage tests reject post-cutoff outcomes, final cancellation reasons, future notes, and actions after the scoring timestamp.",
    "LightGBM fits only on training data and sigmoid calibration fits only on the distinct calibration partition unless prespecified evidence supports isotonic without overfit.",
    "The artifact gate reports calibration, Brier score, PR-AUC, workload at K, required baselines, subgroup counts and performance, and reproducible seeds.",
    "Failure of a prespecified calibration, top-K, or subgroup-harm gate rejects the artifact.",
    "The versioned artifact set contains the model, calibrator, schema, generator version and seed, training time, thresholds, evaluation manifest, and a synthetic-data limitations card.",
    "Camila's held-out T-7, T-2, and T-1 path runs through the normal pipeline and is proven not to contain a hard-coded score, explanation, or channel choice.",
    "The staff UI separates calibrated probability from dated SHAP-margin associations and labels them as associations rather than causes.",
    "Explicit patient response supersedes prediction, and missing, stale, malformed, or incompatible artifacts show Score unavailable while deterministic cadence continues."
  ],
  "created_by": "human"
